 res←file Get y;R_;scalar;o;sheets
⍝ file can be either a name or an IWorkbook object (returned by Open)
⍝ sheets o←y #.PLUS.unopt{EmptyOnError←0 ⋄ EmptyOnNull←0 ⋄ EmptyToChars←0 ⋄ ScalarToVector←0 ⋄ EvaluateFormulas←0}#.uc'n'
sheets←y
o←(EmptyOnError:0 ⋄ EmptyOnNull:0 ⋄ EmptyToChars:0 ⋄ ScalarToVector:0 ⋄ EvaluateFormulas:0)

⍝ sheets is an array of sheet definitions
⍝    or a single (non-nested) sheet definition
⍝    or a single sheet name
⍝    or a list of sheet names
⍝ a sheet definition is
⍝ [1] name [2] first row, origin 1 (default 1) [3] first column, origin 1 (default 1) [4] max rows (default: all available) [5] max cols (default: all available)

⍝ R_←{1:_←⎕WA}#.uDefer ⍬

 :If #.IsChar sheets
 :OrIf (≡sheets)∊1 ¯2
     sheets←⊂sheets
     scalar←1
 :Else
     scalar←⊃0=⍴⍴sheets
 :EndIf

 sheets←{
     ⊂⍣(#.IsChar ⍵)⊢⍵
 }¨sheets

 res←file(o Get_)sheets
 res←''(⍴⍣(scalar∧1≡≢res))res

 :If 0≠⎕NC 'R_.DO'
     R_.DO ⍝ Force GC to close the file.
 :EndIf
 ⍝ I tried all sort of :Disposable but they only slow down the procedure while doing nothing for this resource leak
